# pattern-size-made-at-run-time: a Text Pattern made at run time, by
# splicing, compiles at its `make-pattern`, and one over the Script's
# patternSize is a Limit Fault there, with limit `pattern` (spec chapter 6,
# Limits; chapter 8, Compiling). With patternSize 50, splicing the
# 30-instruction `<29 digits>` after "x" gives 31 instructions and is made,
# and splicing it twice gives 59 and faults. `make-pattern` checks the size
# before its charge, so the fault is on `pattern`, and the 59-instruction
# program is never charged (chapter 8, Charging). The fault, its
# instruction and the rollback of `status` are pinned. Its Fuel, allocation
# and state figures are Cost Model 0's, as the TS Core blessed them.

> load maker identity=7d1bad29ae6f001af7207221ff3d18dcd365a0efd0a129946be58fc54e921bef

# The spliced pattern is a nested group in the canonical source.
> deliver d1 to=maker message=small
> pump clock=2026-09-30T09:00:00Z
seg maker/r1 start delivery=d1 handler=small clause=1 fuel=92 alloc=264 state=540 end=return
run maker/r1 outcome=completed delivery=d1 handler=small fuel=92 alloc=264
pumped state=idle fuel=92

# `status` was written earlier in the Segment, so the rollback restores it.
# `made` is never written, and keeps the pattern from d1.
> deliver d2 to=maker message=big
> pump clock=2026-09-30T09:00:01Z
fault maker/r2 limit=pattern at=maker:18 pos=18:7 rollback=[status]
seg maker/r2 start delivery=d2 handler=big clause=1 fuel=9 alloc=0 state=540 end=fault
run maker/r2 outcome=limit-fault delivery=d2 handler=big limit=pattern fuel=9 alloc=0
pumped state=idle fuel=9

> vars
vars maker unit=<29 digits> status="idle" made=<"x", <29 digits>>
